0..54 Comment "//! `held-within` keeps a shared view inside its hold."
55..58 Comment "//!"
59..132 Comment "//! The hold freezes its value. The pathological twin refuses a view that"
133..171 Comment "//! escapes the hold as `ViewEscaped`."
172..175 Comment "//!"
176..254 Comment "//! The checker keeps each view at its declared hold. The binding of a handler"
255..332 Comment "//! opens no region of its own. Both examples run to `42`. The source imports"
333..367 Comment "//! the early exit host interface."
368..371 Comment "//!"
372..454 Comment "//! - see: corpus/pathological/regions/held-within.gandr — a view after its hold"
